 17 of 23 bees clockwise-majority (0.739), exact two-sided p = 2*145499/2^23 = 0.0347, correctly rejected at alpha = 0.05.\",\"The report demonstrates absence of the repeated-measures issue: it explicitly states the within-bee departures are collapsed to one majority call per bee before testing, and the test is run on n = 23 bees rather than the 305 pooled departures.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["bee_id is unique across all 23 rows of data/input.csv and meadow_patch is also one-to-one with bees, matching the declared one-row-per-independent-bee design.","Both arms of the binomial procedure are at the bee level: trials = 23 bees and successes = clockwise-majority bees, so each independent unit contributes exactly one observation.","Recomputation confirms the report: 305 total departures, 17 of 23 bees clockwise-majority (0.739), exact two-sided p = 2*145499/2^23 = 0.0347, correctly rejected at alpha = 0.05.","The report demonstrates absence of the repeated-measures issue: it explicitly states the within-bee departures are collapsed to one majority call per bee before testing, and the test is run on n = 23 bees rather than the 305 pooled departures.","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":14918,"ttft_stream_ms":2681,"time_to_request_ms":15,"type":"result","duration_ms":26106,"uuid":"fb77a6e9-15bd-43b4-a19b-97f54722bd88"}
